{
  "_about": "Approved news sources for the live feed (approved 2026-10-29). Fetched by source, not per candidate. scope: national (matches any tracked contest) | state (matches only its own state's contests; the state name counts as context) | local (same, plus jurisdiction terms the article may omit). Inclusion rule: original reporting, a public corrections policy, and no ownership or control by a party, campaign, PAC or litigation group; national outlets are chosen across the political spectrum; every outlet that meets the rule is treated the same. Opinion and sponsored items are held by the automated checks. Excluded: CNN and Reuters (no maintained public RSS), RealClearPolitics (aggregator: links to other outlets' stories), Democracy Docket and similar (run by a litigation or advocacy group). Feed URLs follow each outlet's published feed pattern and are confirmed by the collector's first run (feed_source_state.last_status); failing sources back off automatically, and enabled=false drops a source instantly. Outlets that block automated readers (HTTP 403) are turned off with a disabledReason, never worked around (owner, 2026-10-29). Moved feeds are found automatically from the outlet's own advertised feed links (src/lib/feeds/discover.ts). gdeltDomain (owner, 2026-10-30): outlets whose article pages we can't read are also searched by candidate name through GDELT, which reads the article for us; the New York Times through its own Article Search API (src/lib/feeds/apis.ts).",
